WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.820
Just as the night is dark and full of terrors,
the internet is vast and full of spoilers.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.020
Game of Thrones has but two episodes remaining
in its epic eight-season run on television,

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.020
and thanks to a series of purported leaks,
fans may already have the answer as to how

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.060
the show will end.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.760
Naturally, beware of some potentially massive
spoilers for the final episodes of the show.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.360
Leaks for Game of Thrones season 8 began surfacing
online several months before the series returned

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.820
to HBO in April, and have continued to crop
up on various forums as the season has aired.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.240
That leaked information has been compiled
by the Game of Thrones subreddit /r/freefolk,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.050
with a recent update including potential details
about the last half of the final season.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.960
Though many were initially hesitant to take
the leaks at face value, information provided

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.020
about episode 4 of the season wound up being
startlingly accurate.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.330
With that in mind, people have become much
more inclined to believe the leaks about the

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.280
last two episodes are true.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.019
According to the post on Reddit, the remaining
episodes of Game of Thrones season 8 will

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.240
allegedly feature the following developments,
not necessarily in this order.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.600
Now's the time to look away.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.620
Daenerys and her army will capture Jaime Lannister,
who was last seen heading back to King's Landing.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.080
Dany also gives orders to execute Varys, presumably
for committing treason with his increasing

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.020
inclinations toward supporting Jon Snow and
protecting the citizens of the realm.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.040
"I will act in their interest no matter the
personal cost."

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.080
He is reportedly burned alive.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.800
All the while, Tyrion begs Daenerys to show
mercy, and attempts to resign as Hand, which

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.740
she refuses.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.200
Jon Snow also attempts to reason with her,
and fails.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:50.020
Instead of keeping a cool head in the face
of resistance, something snaps in Dany, and

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.780
she decides to storm King's Landing against
her advisors' wishes.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.180
Her forces easily take the city in a one-sided
fight, and she also finally gets her chance

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.280
to light up Euron Greyjoy and the Iron Fleet.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.740
From there, the leaked information alleges
that Daenerys and her Unsullied army will

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.980
dole out extreme violence in King's Landing,
further alienating Tyrion and Jon.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.480
She begins executing many people.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.180
Fed up with Daenerys' increasingly unhinged
actions, Tyrion frees Jaime and even attempts

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.280
to get Cersei to safety as well.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:27.110
The leaks also claim that the chaos in King's
Landing will serve as the backdrop to the

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:32.180
long-awaited Clegane Bowl also known as the
battle between brothers the Hound and the

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:32.680
Mountain.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.080
Both characters apparently die in the conflict.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.580
The Mother of Dragons, apparently now in full
Mad Queen mode, arrests Tyrion for freeing

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.120
Jaime and sentences him to be executed.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.960
Tyrion then allegedly does a complete 180
on his allegiance to Daenerys, and begins

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.280
attempting to convince Jon to turn on her.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.280
In his view, Jon and the Stark family will
never be safe from an unhinged Daenerys, because

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.860
Jon's claim to the Throne serves as a threat
to her legitimacy.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.440
Jon tries to talk to her, but is ignored,
with Daenerys believing her actions are justified.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:11.260
With that avenue exhausted, Tyrion teams up
with Sansa to devise a plan to overthrow Dany

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.960
and turn Jon against her.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.220
Despite agreeing to the plot at first, Sansa
ultimately betrays Tyrion.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.920
"I used to think you were the cleverest man
alive."

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.860
Tyrion's trial is said to take place in the
Dragonpit, and is said to have Samwell Tarly,

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:30.360
Brienne of Tarth, Grey Worm, and Robin Arryn
of all people in attendance, among others.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:36.060
Tyrion gives an enraged and resentful monologue,
criticizing the onlookers for turning against

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.620
him despite his many sacrifices for the people
of King's Landing.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.220
But he can't talk his way out of this one.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.580
He slumps to his knees, defeated.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.620
Though the details aren't clear yet, he reportedly
dies.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.040
That's not all.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:55.099
Additionally, Jaime will fight Euron, killing
the crazed Greyjoy man but sustaining fatal

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.140
injuries himself.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.300
Jaime is said to make his way back to Cersei,
and the two die together, though who kills

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.460
who and why is still unknown.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:08.780
Finally, the leaks make a bold claim about
how Jon and Dany's story ends.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:12.920
After failing to get through to Daenerys and
make her see that her sack of King's Landing

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.400
was wrong, Jon ultimately kills her.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:20.940
According to the purported leaks, Kit Harington
shot two possible endings for his character,

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:25.340
so Jon will either take the black and join
a new Night's Watch, or will die before the

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.840
end of the final episode.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.860
This information reportedly comes from several
different sources that mostly corroborate

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.420
each other, though some leaks have information
that other sources don't.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.130
According to one leak, the series will end
with a council deciding that Bran should rule

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.360
the Seven Kingdoms.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:47.400
Sansa will rule the North, and Samwell, Bronn,
and Ser Davos will serve as Bran's advisers.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:51.660
Interestingly, this leak also insists that
Tyrion will be among Bran's advisers, Tyrion

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.740
will be among Bran's advisers, contradicting
the other leaks that say he dies.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:59.340
It also seems to contradict Bran's previous
statements about desiring any kind of power

00:04:59.340 --> 00:04:59.960
at all.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.080
And that's it that's the information that's
out there.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:07.740
Parts of it may well be true, and other parts
may be deliberate misinformation seeded by

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.200
the production to muddy the spoiler waters.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:14.360
Either way, it sounds like an ending that's
determined to frustrate, ending the series

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.000
on what sounds like an incredibly divisive
note.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.680
Only time will tell, but if the bulk of these
turn out to be accurate, let's just say that

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.840
King's Landing isn't the only thing that will
go up in flames the internet probably will,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:27.340
too.

